10766       * Source: S154 / Chapter 33 / `PATHDIAGRAM Statement` (PDF pp. 1626–1638); S154 / Chapter 33 / `Path Diagrams: Layout Algorithms, Default
10766    ! Settings, and Customization` (PDF pp. 1735–1757).
10767       * Discriminates: Example 33.17: Path Analysis: Stability of Alienation; explicit statements: PATHDIAGRAM
10768       */
10769      options nosyntaxcheck obs=max firstobs=1 nodate nonumber nocenter linesize=160 pagesize=max nostimer nofullstimer validvarname=v7
10769    ! validmemname=compatible locale=en_US;
10770      %let syscc=0;
10771      title; footnote;
10772      ods _all_ close;
10773      ods listing gpath="%sysfunc(pathname(work))";
10774      ods graphics off;
10775      proc datasets library=work kill nolist;
NOTE: Deleting WORK.REGSTRY (memtype=ITEMSTOR).
NOTE: File WORK.REGSTRY (memtype=ITEMSTOR) cannot be deleted because it is in use.
NOTE: Deleting WORK.SASGOPT (memtype=CATALOG).
NOTE: File WORK.SASGOPT (memtype=CATALOG) cannot be deleted because it is in use.
NOTE: Deleting WORK.SASMAC1 (memtype=CATALOG).
NOTE: File WORK.SASMAC1 (memtype=CATALOG) cannot be deleted because it is in use.
NOTE: Deleting WORK.TEMPLAT (memtype=ITEMSTOR).
